# style-convert

## Project Overview
- **Purpose:** Apply visual styles from a reference image onto a target image using an LLM, then deliver the result as an Adobe Illustrator (`.ai`) file
- **Type:** REST API
- **Domain:** AI-powered image transformation and file conversion
- **Stack:** FastAPI, Python, Claude API (vision), Convertio API

## Core Features
- **Style Transfer** — accepts a style reference image, a target image, and a prompt; returns a styled PNG via LLM
- **Format Conversion** — converts the LLM-generated PNG to `.ai` format via Convertio API
- **Single Endpoint Flow** — the full pipeline (style → convert) is triggered from one request and returns a downloadable `.ai` file

## Pipeline Flow

```
Client
  │
  ▼
POST /convert
  │  ├── style_reference (image)
  ├── target_image (image)
  └── prompt (string)
        │
        ▼
  [ Step 1: LLM — Style Transfer ]
  │  Input : style_reference + target_image + prompt
  │  Model : Claude (vision)
  │  Output: styled PNG (bytes)
        │
        ▼
  [ Step 2: Convertio API — Format Conversion ]
  │  Input : styled PNG (bytes)
  │  Output: .ai file (bytes)
        │
        ▼
Client receives .ai file download
```

## Domain Model

```
ConvertRequest
├── style_reference   # uploaded image — style source (jpg/png)
├── target_image      # uploaded image — image to be modified (jpg/png)
├── prompt            # string — instructions to guide the style transfer

ConvertResponse
├── file              # .ai file as a downloadable binary response
├── filename          # generated output filename (e.g. output_<uuid>.ai)
```

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── main.py                  # FastAPI app entry point, router registration
├── routers/
│   └── convert.py           # POST /convert endpoint
├── services/
│   ├── llm_service.py       # Claude API call — style transfer, returns PNG bytes
│   └── convertio_service.py # Convertio API call — PNG to .ai conversion
├── schemas/
